{
 "_about": "The missions, as a tree (Sam, 2026-10-05: \"the tree structure of vagrancy for the missions with different unlock reqs\"). After Vagrancy's data/road.json: a mission opens when every one of its requirements is met, and the row a mission sits in is how many it has; a requirement names only a mission with fewer requirements, so the tree runs downward. Requirements: pass a mission; average at least a mark on it (mark); pass it with waste under a share (clean). A mission has one line or two (Sam: \"levels with multiple conveyer belts\"), each with its belt, cup, spouts, orders and conditions; with two, the first is the upper line. Order parts are written in the order the sentence names them. builds_on lists edges of data/kc_graph.json. Side paths (Sam, 2026-10-06: \"paths that only have one pre-req per level that are on a differnet path than the main line\"): missions whose ids start s_ each have one requirement, chained within their chapter; the tree places every mission by its depth, one more than the deepest mission it requires.",
